一起跑通 Run It Through · Persona Pop (拟人 MV), a NEO-Cine library demo

UNOFFICIAL FAN FILM: the two characters, 小克 (Klaude) and 扣扣 (Kodex), are original drawings named after two real AI coding
  assistants, Claude (Anthropic) and Codex (OpenAI). No logo, mascot or interface of either product is drawn; the names
  appear on name chips and in the lyrics only. The film is not made, endorsed or reviewed by Anthropic or OpenAI. Claude and
  Codex are names of their owners and are not licensed here.

CHARACTERS: generated by the library's author with the Codex CLI's built-in image tool (image_gen), 2026-11-22, from the
  character sheets and prompts in cast.json (style, look, and one prompt per pose; every pose after the first was generated
  with the character's reference sheet attached). 18 images: 12 full-figure poses, 6 chest-up close-ups, each on a magenta
  ground; then, 2026-11-23, two 2×2 mouth sheets on a transparent background, each generated with its close-up attached.
  ../kit/tools/key.py turns them into assets/chars/*.webp and meta.json (in git): keying, one scale per character measured
  on the head, the sheets cut into 8 aligned cells. The originals (cast/raw/, about 30 MB) are kept out of git.

MUSIC AND SOUND: no recordings, no samples, no voice. The backing (chip-pop: drums, bass, arpeggio, pad) and the lead that
  "sings" the lyrics, one note per glyph, are synthesized with numpy by ../kit/tools/mix.py from mv.json and the picture's
  events; the sound effects come from the library's core/audio/sfx.py and from mix.py, each placed on its picture event.

LYRICS AND STORY: by the library's author (mv.json, sheet).

